    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d131">

                <pb facs="0130" n="122" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg122"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.24/626</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Chief of the Division of
                        the American Republics</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Walmsley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-27">October 27, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Cuban Ambassador, Dr. Concheso, called today at his own request to inform the
                    Department that the President of Cuba had approved the third draft of the Lend
                    Lease contract providing for arms deliveries valued at $7,200,000 and had
                    authorized him, the Ambassador, to sign.</p>
                <p>Will you<anchor n="42" xml:id="d131-f1"/> please notify the Treaty Division and
                    have the other details taken care of so that signature may be effected as soon
                    as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. N. Walmsley,
                    Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d131-f1" n="42" xml:id="d131-f1-content">
                <p>Apparently Mr. John S. Hooker, Assistant Executive Secretary, Board of Economic
                    Operations.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
